## Self-Correction

### How Agents Detect and Fix Mistakes

Cursor agents have built-in self-correction mechanisms:

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Execute tool] --> B{Result success?}
    B -->|Yes| C[Continue to next step]
    B -->|No| D[Analyze failure]
    
    D --> E{Error type?}
    E -->|Tool error| F[Retry with different parameters]
    E -->|Content error| G[Read correct section]
    E -->|Logic error| H[Re-plan approach]
    E -->|Permission error| I[Ask user for approval]
    
    F --> J[Retry]
    G --> J
    H --> K[New plan]
    I --> L[Wait for user]
    
    J --> M{Second attempt success?}
    M -->|Yes| C
    M -->|No| N[Report error to user]
    L --> C
```

### Self-Correction Patterns

| Pattern | When Used | Example |
|---------|-----------|---------|
| **Retry with different params** | Tool call failed | Grep failed → try broader pattern |
| **Read before edit** | Uncertain content | StrReplace failed → Read file → correct edit |
| **Backtrack** | Change caused error | Undo last change → try different approach |
| **Simplify** | Complex approach failing | Break into smaller steps |
| **Alternative tool** | Primary tool insufficient | Grep not enough → use SemanticSearch |

### Debugging Self-Correction (Verbose Mode)

```json
{
  "cursor.agent.logLevel": "verbose",
  "cursor.agent.debugLogging": true
}
```

With verbose logging, self-correction is visible:

```
[DEBUG] Tool: Read(file="src/auth.ts")
[DEBUG] Result: 45 lines read
[DEBUG] Thought: Need to verify middleware import exists...
[DEBUG] Tool: Grep(pattern="import.*authMiddleware", path="src/auth.ts")
[DEBUG] Result: 0 matches found
[DEBUG] Thought: Import not found, adding it...
[DEBUG] Tool: StrReplace(file="src/auth.ts", old="...", new="...")
[DEBUG] Result: 1 replacement made
[DEBUG] Tool: Read(file="src/auth.ts", offset=1, limit=10)
[DEBUG] Result: Verified import added at line 2
[DEBUG] Thought: Import confirmed, continuing...
```

