## Agent Autonomy Levels

### What Agents Can Do Without Confirmation

| Action | Auto-Execute | Review Needed | Approval Needed |
|--------|-------------|---------------|----------------|
| **Read files** | ✅ Yes | ❌ No | ❌ No |
| **Grep/Search** | ✅ Yes | ❌ No | ❌ No |
| **Edit single file** | ✅ Yes | ⚠️ Output visible | ❌ No |
| **Write new file** | ✅ Yes | ⚠️ Output visible | ❌ No |
| **Shell (read-only)** | ✅ Yes | ⚠️ Output visible | ❌ No |
| **Shell (build/test)** | ✅ Yes | ⚠️ Output visible | ❌ No |
| **Shell (install)** | ⚠️ May ask | ✅ Recommended | ❌ No |
| **Multiple file edits** | ⚠️ May ask | ✅ Recommended | ❌ No |
| **Security changes** | ❌ No | ✅ Required | ✅ Required |
| **Infrastructure changes** | ❌ No | ✅ Required | ✅ Required |
| **Delete files** | ❌ No | ✅ Required | ⚠️ Sometimes |

### Configuring Autonomy

```json
{
  // Auto-approve agent actions
  "cursor.agent.autoApprove": false,
  
  // Minimum approval level for actions
  "cursor.agent.minApprovalLevel": "medium", // "low", "medium", "high"
  
  // Actions that always require approval
  "cursor.agent.approvalRequired": [
    "Shell(command: *install*)",
    "Shell(command: *rm*)",
    "Shell(command: *sudo*)",
    "Delete",
    "StrReplace(pattern: *security*)"
  ]
}
```

