## Relationship to Subagents

### When Agent Spawns Subagent vs Doing Work Itself

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Main Agent receives task] --> B{Task complexity?}
    B -->|Simple, single file| C[Agent handles directly]
    B -->|Complex, multi-domain| D[Spawn subagent]
    
    D --> E{Task type?}
    E -->|Code exploration| F[explore subagent]
    E -->|Code quality review| G[bugbot subagent]
    E -->|Security review| H[security-review subagent]
    E -->|CI failure analysis| I[ci-investigator subagent]
    E -->|Parallel implementation| J[best-of-n-runner]
    E -->|General complex task| K[generalPurpose subagent]
    
    C --> L[Direct execution]
    F --> M[Results returned to main agent]
    G --> M
    H --> M
    I --> M
    J --> M
    K --> M
```

### Subagent Decision Matrix

| Task | Direct Agent | Subagent |
|------|-------------|----------|
| Edit 1-2 files | ✅ | ❌ |
| Research a codebase area | ⚠️ | ✅ explore subagent |
| Security review | ⚠️ | ✅ security-review subagent |
| Code quality review | ⚠️ | ✅ bugbot subagent |
| Parallel implementations | ❌ | ✅ best-of-n-runner |
| Multi-domain expertise | ⚠️ | ✅ generalPurpose subagent |

